   - run_many joins the stopper with timeout=5 (run.py:1640).
   Per the new Interrupts paragraph:
   - the stopper blocks in Event.wait(), with no polling loop (run.py:56-64 spins at 100% CPU);
   - it runs the stop sequences of all running groups concurrently;
   - a group started after the flag also gets a stop sequence;
   - run_many joins the stopper with no timeout and returns only when every group is gone.
   Tests: the grandchild input above must leave no live group after run_many returns. Three SIGINT-ignoring children must all get their SIGINT within 1 s of the flag.

